{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"SnowplowEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"SnowplowEncoding"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint with a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 25"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for a collector URL that isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":", that has no host,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Schemas from the tracking plan","level":3,"anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan’s own check does:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"export writes it as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"text":", then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-2"},{"text":", each listing the earlier ones in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$supersedes"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow validates events naming ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"text":" alone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the registry from the plan with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>"},{"type":"text","text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"export-tracking-plan"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-vendor"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"--iglu-registry"},{"type":"text","text":". Then publish it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igluctl"},{"type":"text","text":" before the release that sends the events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"text":", and the version must be 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What Snowplow receives","level":3,"anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a "},{"code":"payload_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": a self-describing event, with its data in "},{"code":"ue_pr","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as JSON text;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event was tracked;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the app ID; "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform; "},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; and "},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"},{"type":"text","text":" as Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile_context"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-3"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" for a record with no device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Only the session identifies a record","level":3,"anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Snowplow’s "},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else identifies it. No "},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, no "},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity (its "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one a store recovered after a relaunch, is sent without a "},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read a session from the "},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity, so set the unified package’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"snowplow__session_identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"code":"sp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SP-Anonymous: *","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"code":"network_userid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","level":3,"anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"might not take with the request around it."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What the collector doesn’t report","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_id"},{"type":"text","text":", count it once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowSetupError":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowsetuperror","title":"SnowplowSetupError","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t be made."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnowplowSetupError"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnowplowSetupError"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"type":"topic","title":"BatchEncoder","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"type":"topic","title":"batchLimit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s trackers’ limits on one request, 25 events and 40,000 bytes of body, and an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of up to 150,000 bytes in a request of its own."}],"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/batchlimit","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collector"},{"type":"text","text":", as self-describing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events whose schemas are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":"’s under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendor"},{"type":"text","text":", from the app "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"type":"text","text":", through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"snowplow","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"collector","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20Foundatio